// slot-rebind reference-analysis gap coverage (defensive correctness hardening).
// `slot-rebind.no` already exercises the happy-path rebind + degrade-to-copy.
// This file isolates constructs the *source-reference* scanner must walk so that a
// later write to the move source forces a value-copy (not a 0-copy stack-slot
// rebind, which would alias and corrupt the target).
//
// NOTE: for-range (`i <- [..]`) is intentionally NOT used here because the
// in-tree on-demand-std transpiler refactor (WIP, out of scope for slot-rebind)
// currently fails to preload `fmt` for `print` inside a for-range body; that is a
// separate transpiler bug, not a rebind bug. The IterRange gap is covered by code
// inspection of stmtContainsVarRefAny (ForStatement.IterRange.

// (1) bare block that writes the move source: BlockStatement must be scanned.
a = 5
b = a
{
    a = 7
}
print(b)   // expect 5 (rebind disabled: a written inside block; b is an independent copy)

// (2) read-only reference of the source after the move: safe to keep the
//     optimization; the value is preserved.
x = 42
y = x
print(y)   // expect 42

// (3) degenerate: source written again after the move in the open scope.
p = 9
q = p
p = 1
print(q)   // expect 9 (rebind disabled: p reassigned after move)
